Package: ggbasket
Type: Package
Title: Learn from Basketball Games: NBA and EuroLeague Play-by-Play, Metrics and Graphics
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R: person("Loukas", "Theodosiou", email = "loukesio@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Reads NBA (ESPN, via 'hoopR') and EuroLeague (official live
    API) play-by-play into one layout with the players on court, and turns
    it into box scores, game flow and scoring runs, win probability,
    four-factor explanations of a result, on/off and line-up ratings,
    game-to-game consistency, clutch splits, assist networks and the effect
    of pressure on shooting. Also provides team, player and shot metrics
    (possessions, ratings, rate statistics, Pythagorean wins, shrunken
    shooting rates, expected field-goal percentage) and story-first 'ggplot2'
    graphics on NBA and FIBA courts. Started as a redesign of the analyses
    in Zuccolotto and Manisera (2020) "Basketball Data Science".
URL: https://loukesio.github.io/ggbasket/, https://github.com/loukesio/ggbasket
BugReports: https://github.com/loukesio/ggbasket/issues
